title: '[pallet-revive] Reject calls from a fallback account shadowed by a mapping'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Calling or instantiating a contract now fails with `BadOrigin` when the origin is an
    eth-derived account whose address has been mapped to a native account. This happens when a
    native account is mapped and then acts through its fallback account, for example via
    `dispatch_as_fallback_account`. The fallback account shares the mapped address but not its
    nonce or balance, so it used to derive CREATE1 addresses from a second nonce and pay with
    funds the EVM does not attribute to that address.

    The check applies to every entry point: the `call`, `instantiate` and
    `instantiate_with_code` extrinsics, `Pallet::bare_call` and `Pallet::bare_instantiate`
    (used, for example, by XCM asset transactors), and the `call` and `instantiate` runtime
    APIs, so a dry run reports the same error. No migration or API change is needed.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    A mapped account can no longer call or deploy contracts as its fallback account. Funds held
    by the fallback account can still be recovered by dispatching calls to other pallets, such as
    a balance transfer, through `dispatch_as_fallback_account`.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
